# Template for .env — copy it with `cp .env.example .env` and fill in the values,
# or leave .env absent: app.py generates both secrets on first start and appends them to .env (mode 600).
# Never commit .env (it is in .gitignore). A value set in the process environment overrides .env.
# Format: one KEY=value per line, no quotes, no spaces around "=".
#
# CARLOS_DATA — optional: the data directory (database, photos, backups, dossiers). Default: ./data next to the code.
# Set it in the process environment (it is read before .env is loaded), e.g. CARLOS_DATA=/srv/carlos-data python app.py

# AGENT_TOKEN — the first admin's agent token for the write API (/api/agent/*) until a token is generated in the UI
# (Settings → account → new token). Other accounts get their own token the same way.
# Sent as the HTTP header:  Authorization: Bearer <AGENT_TOKEN>
# Gives full write access to the database through the API (inserts, corrections, photo uploads),
# so keep it long and random. Generate one with:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Without it the agent API answers 403.
AGENT_TOKEN=
